      "worked": "Since $\\sqrt{1+x^2}>|x|$, both $\\sqrt{1+x^2}+x$ and $\\sqrt{1+x^2}-x$ are positive for every real $x$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=\\ln\\left(\\sqrt{1+x^2}-x\\right)\\\\f(-x)&=\\ln\\left(\\frac{(\\sqrt{1+x^2}-x)(\\sqrt{1+x^2}+x)}{\\sqrt{1+x^2}+x}\\right)\\\\f(-x)&=\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+x^2}+x}\\right)\\\\f(-x)&=-\\ln\\left(\\sqrt{1+x^2}+x\\right)\\\\f(-x)&=-f(x).\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $f$ is an odd function.",
